.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.PP
.nf
A mixin class for any class (a TreeBuilder, or some class used by a
TreeBuilder) that's in a position to detect whether an XML
document is being incorrectly parsed as HTML, and issue an
appropriate warning\&.

This requires being able to observe an incoming processing
instruction that might be an XML declaration, and also able to
observe tags as they're opened\&. If you can't do that for a given
`TreeBuilder`, there's a less reliable implementation based on
examining the raw markup\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS " None bs4\&.builder\&.DetectsXMLParsedAsHTML\&._document_might_be_xml ( self, str processing_instruction)\fC [protected]\fP"

.PP
.nf
Call this method when encountering an XML declaration, or a
'processing instruction' that might be an XML declaration\&.

This helps Beautiful Soup detect potential issues later, if
the XML document turns out to be a non-XHTML document that's
being parsed as XML\&.

.fi
.PP
 
