.PP
.nf
Call this method before parsing a document\&.
.fi
.PP
 
.SS " None bs4\&.builder\&.DetectsXMLParsedAsHTML\&._root_tag_encountered ( self, str name)\fC [protected]\fP"

.PP
.nf
Call this when you encounter the document's root tag\&.

This is where we actually check whether an XML document is
being incorrectly parsed as HTML, and issue the warning\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " None bs4\&.builder\&.DetectsXMLParsedAsHTML\&._warn ( cls, int  stacklevel = \fC5\fP)\fC [protected]\fP"

.PP
.nf
Issue a warning about XML being parsed as HTML\&.
.fi
.PP
 
.SS " bool bs4\&.builder\&.DetectsXMLParsedAsHTML\&.warn_if_markup_looks_like_xml ( cls, Optional[_RawMarkup] markup, int  stacklevel = \fC3\fP)"

.PP
.nf
Perform a check on some markup to see if it looks like XML
that's not XHTML\&. If so, issue a warning\&.

This is much less reliable than doing the check while parsing,
but some of the tree builders can't do that\&.

:param stacklevel: The stacklevel of the code calling this\\
 function\&.

:return: True if the markup looks like non-XHTML XML, False
 otherwise\&.

.fi
.PP
 
